```

Replace invuln flicker block with just visibility flicker, decrement only in timers. Add dying physics and finished celebration.

Let me restructure:

```js
    this.player.visible = this.invuln > 0 ? Math.floor(this.time * 18) % 2 === 0 : true

    // jump physics
    if (this.state === 'running' || this.state === 'ready' || this.state === 'dying') {
      if (!this.grounded) { ... gravity ... }
      if (this.landPulse > 0) this.landPulse -= dt
    }
```
But landing callback during dying would fire onLand; fine. Actually playerY set to 0 in takeHit, grounded false with vy=8 -> jumps up a bit while tumbling. Fun.

In dying state, if landing sets grounded true, no more. Fine.

Finished: add bounce:
```js
if (this.state === 'finished') {
  this.playerY = Math.abs(Math.sin(this.finishT * 3.4)) * 0.32
}
```
Arms pose: in arms loop, target depends on finished/idle. Add:
```js
const celebrate = this.state === 'finished'
...
const target = celebrate ? -2.5 : lerp(armSwing*dir, 0.5, s)
```
legs for finished maybe small bounce; leave.

Body lean: rig.rotation.x target lerp(-0.13, 1.32, s) for finished should 0? Use celebrate ? -0.05. Current s=0 so -0.13; fine but arms up.

Also idle attract pose with arms slight. fine.

Stumble: remove extra decrement. Keep stumble decrement in update speed branch only when running. It starts 1.1 decays there. Good.

Also `this.player.visible` on death: flicker only when invuln>0. Fine.

Apply.

