- Record guide samples. Then call render? updateHud is called by emitHud every 0.055 game time, so after loop HUD reflects last state; if guide at last frame null, guide HUD off. We can capture after each step when guide not null. Use the last guide frame and then evaluate DOM right after a step where guide exists. Better:

```
const g=window.__templeGame;
g.invuln=1e9;
const seen=[];
window.__guideSnapshot=null;
for (let i=0;i<1800;i++){
  g.update(1/60);
  if (g.guide) { seen.push({action:g.guide.action,distance:g.guide.distance,urgent:g.guide.urgent,lane:g.laneIndex}); window.__guideSnapshot={...g.guide}; }
  if (seen.length>40) break;
}
// HUD should render the last guide; call one more emit? emitHud is public-ish:
g.emitHud(true);
return {...}
```
`emitHud(true)` will call onHud with current g.guide. If guide null at that moment, HUD off. Instead, when we encounter a guide, break immediately and call `g.emitHud(true)`. But guide updates each frame; simply break on first non-null, then emitHud(true). Then inspect DOM. That guarantees guide HUD on.

Then test urgent by continuing stepping until distance <=7 if first guide distance maybe 30. Loop until `g.guide?.urgent` then emitHud and check `.is-urgent`.

Guide may not appear if all obstacles spawn in other lanes; within 25s there will be several. The `updateGuide` returns null when nearest obstacle not in lane; but over 1800 frames definitely obstacles in lane 1. Should be fine.

Test lane movement: after first guide, dispatch 'a' and step one frame; check g.laneIndex and HUD lanes. But moving lane may change guide. Do at end.

Also check touch hint: guide action `jump` highlights `.touch-btn[data-action="jump"]`. `renderGuide` adds `is-hint` to matching. Check.

Let's rewrite the duringRun portion. Use evaluate returning guide history and DOM snapshot after forced emit. But note `g.emitHud(true)` calls onHud → updateHud → renderGuide uses app.dataset.view. Fine.

Also there's `countdown` timers; not relevant.

Let's modify the script carefully.

